///1PIP
Help by Willem Aandewiel
PIP - Copy files under CP/M-86

///2SYNTAX
  PIP destination=source

Destination comes first. Existing files can be replaced.

  A>PIP B:COPY.TXT=A:NOTES.TXT

///2MULTIPLE
  A>PIP B:=A:*.HLP[V]

Copies matching files; V verifies written data.

///2BINARY
  A>PIP B:=A:HELP.CMD[OV]
  A>PIP B:=A:CPMHELP.HLP[OV]

O preserves binary data containing Ctrl-Z. V adds verification.
Use OV for indexed HLP files as well as executable files.

///2TEXT
  A>PIP ALL.TXT=PART1.TXT,PART2.TXT

Combines text in the specified order.

///2INTERACTIVE
PIP alone opens its * prompt.
Enter copying commands there; an empty line exits.
